    "query": "What are the best small colleges in New England?",
    "response": "**Liberal Arts Colleges:**\n\n* **Amherst College (Amherst, MA)**\n  * Known for its rigorous academics, vibrant campus community, and beautiful setting in the Pioneer Valley.\n* **Williams College (Williamstown, MA)**\n  * Consistently ranked among the top liberal arts colleges in the nation, known for its challenging curriculum and picturesque campus in the Berkshires.\n* **Bowdoin College (Brunswick, ME)**\n  * A nationally recognized liberal arts college with strong programs in the humanities, sciences, and social sciences.\n* **Middlebury College (Middlebury, VT)**\n  * Known for its exceptional language programs and beautiful campus in the Green Mountains.\n* **Colby College (Waterville, ME)**\n  * A highly selective liberal arts college with strengths in the sciences and social sciences, located in the idyllic town of Waterville.\n\n**Small Universities with Comprehensive Programs:**\n\n* **Tufts University (Medford/Somerville, MA)**\n  * A small, research-intensive university with a strong liberal arts core and excellent programs in engineering, science, and medicine.\n* **Boston College (Chestnut Hill, MA)**\n  * A Jesuit university with a strong academic reputation and beautiful campus in the Boston suburbs.\n* **Worcester Polytechnic Institute (Worcester, MA)**\n  * A high-tech university with a focus on engineering, computer science, and robotics.\n* **Clark University (Worcester, MA)**\n  * A research-intensive university known for its strengths in psychology, geography, and other social sciences.\n* **Providence College (Providence, RI)**\n  * A private, Catholic university with a strong liberal arts core and excellent programs in business and health sciences.\n\n**Specialized Institutions:**\n\n* **Berklee College of Music (Boston, MA)**\n  * The world's leading contemporary music and performing arts college.\n* **Rhode Island School of Design (Providence, RI)**\n  * One of the top art and design colleges in the country.\n* **Marist College (Poughkeepsie, NY)**\n  * A comprehensive university with strong programs in business, communications, and the arts.\n* **Simmons College (Boston, MA)**\n  * A private women's university known for its health sciences and social work programs.\n* **Mount Holyoke College (South Hadley, MA)**\n  * A prestigious all-women's liberal arts college with a strong focus on the liberal arts.",
